=begin
  demonmana.lic
  A minor demon can hold a little mana (gswiki Minor_Summoning_(725), Minor Demon
  Abilities): base + Demonology bonus / 10 -- an igaesha 12 + 15 = ~28 at a
  bonus of 152, a verlok 0 + (15 - 3) = ~12, an aishan none. Sending costs a bit
  more than arrives and getting it back loses a bit more (10.19: 30 spent -> 28
  stored -> 26 back), but the demon can be filled while you rest and emptied in
  the middle of a hunt. Asking for more than it holds is harmless ("does not have
  that much mana so it resolves to send 28").

    ;demonmana send    send it all the mana it can hold   (mdemon_refresh does this while you rest)
    ;demonmana get     ask it for all of it back          (attack-ultima / sac4mana, once a hunt, when low)

  A `get` never stands waiting while something alive is in the room (it may be your attack script
  that is calling): a demon that isn't there is called, and asked on a later try.

  Which demon, and under what noun, comes from a silent TELL MDEMON RETURN (it also calls
  the demon back to the room first if it had wandered off).

  Sends show how much a demon accepts (its capacity: the most any one send put in it). If
  that's under MIN_STORE (20) the demon is skipped from then on -- no more sends, no get, and
  no waiting for it to arrive -- until it's replaced by a new one, which is measured afresh.

  Silver can be held too; not done here.

  ON unless switched off. (It was off by default from 11/05, when the demon was a verlok holding ~12
  mana, and exited without a word, so from 11/27, with a demon that holds 40, it looked broken.)
  Every caller (mdemon_refresh, attack-ultima, fizzanim, sac4mana, ...) just runs ;demonmana send /
  get, so this one switch stops them all, with no waiting for the demon:
    ;vars set demonmana=off    turn it off
    ;vars set demonmana=on     turn it back on
=end

# Read at run time, so changing it needs no reload.
if UserVars.demonmana.to_s.strip =~ /\A(?:off|0|false|no)\z/i
  echo "switched off: nothing sent or asked for (;vars set demonmana=on turns it back on)."
  exit
end

SEND_OK  = /(\d+) points were succes+fully transferred to your .+? while only draining (\d+) mana points/i
GOT_MANA = /You gain (\d+) mana points/i
GONE     = /could not find|what were you referring/i

# A demon that holds less than this isn't worth the ~30 mana a send costs (10.19: a
# silver verlok'asha held 15 and gave back 7; an igaesha held 28 and gave back 26).
MIN_STORE = 20

# TELL MDEMON RETURN answers with the demon's id, noun and current name -- whatever illusion
# it wears (10.23: an imp as a "gnoll", "wizened gnoll" in the reply, "stooped and wizened
# gnoll" in the room) -- and calls it back if it had wandered off. SEND needs that noun:
# `send 50 gnoll` works, `send 50 mdemon` never does. Replies (all carry the link):
#   But your <a>X</a> is already here!  You're not playing games on it, are you?
#   Your <a>X</a> acknowledges your order and begins to travel to your location.
#   The magic in your location is interfering with your <a>X</a> returning to you.
RETURN_REPLY = /already here!|acknowledges your order|interfering with your|You have no minor demon at this time/i
DEMON_LINK   = %r{(?:[Bb]ut your|Your|your) <pushBold/><a exist="(\d+)" noun="([\w,'-]+)">([\w\-' ]+)</a><popBold/>}
# secs to wait for a called-back demon while resting; GET_WAIT in the middle of a hunt.
# 11.01: from the Den of Rot to the rest room the demon took 65-67s on four sends in a row, none of
# them hurried by the re-sent return order, so a 60s wait missed every time by 4-7s.
ARRIVE_WAIT  = 90
# 10.30 overnight: an imp took 20-26s to catch up after the return order, so a 10s wait gave up on
# 24 of 25 mid-hunt gets. A get that still misses its demon unlatches $demonmana_taken (attack-ultima
# / sac4mana set it before calling us, once a hunt) and tries again after GET_RETRY_AFTER secs,
# by which time the demon is usually here.
GET_WAIT        = 30
GET_RETRY_AFTER = 45

# How often the wait for a lagging demon repeats TELL MDEMON RETURN.
def demonmana_recall_every
  15
end

def here?(id)
  (GameObj.npcs.to_a + GameObj.loot.to_a + GameObj.room_desc.to_a).any? { |o| o.id.to_s == id.to_s }
end

# => { id:, noun:, name:, here: } for your minor demon, or nil (said why). Asked silently.
def demon(wait = ARRIVE_WAIT)
  text = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("tell mdemon return", RETURN_REPLY).to_a.join("\n")
  unless text =~ DEMON_LINK
    echo(text =~ /no minor demon/i ? "you have no minor demon." : "no answer to TELL MDEMON RETURN.")
    return nil
  end
  d = { id: $1, noun: $2, name: $3, here: text.include?("already here!") }
  return d if low_capacity?(d)                      # not worth waiting for
  if text.include?("begins to travel") && wait.positive?
    echo "your #{d[:name]} wasn't here -- waiting for it to arrive."
    wait.times do |i|
      break if (d[:here] = here?(d[:id]))
      if i > 0 && (i % demonmana_recall_every).zero?   # imps stray the most: call it again (11.01)
        again = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("tell mdemon return", RETURN_REPLY).to_a.join("\n")
        break if (d[:here] = again.include?("already here!"))
      end
      sleep 1
    end
  end
  d
end

# What sends to the current demon have shown: { id:, points: } -- the most points one send put in it
# is its capacity (a demon that still held some takes less). A new demon (new id) gets one send to find out.
def low_capacity?(d)
  c = $demonmana_cap
  !!(c && c[:id] == d[:id] && c[:points] < MIN_STORE)
end

def skip_note(d)
  c = $demonmana_cap
  echo "your #{d[:name]} holds only #{c[:points]} mana (under #{MIN_STORE}) -- not worth it, skipping." unless c[:said]
  c[:said] = true
end

def send_mana
  d = demon
  return unless d
  return skip_note(d) if low_capacity?(d)
  return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here -- not sending.") unless d[:here]
  waitrt?
  r = dothistimeout("send 50 #{d[:noun]}", 4, Regexp.union(SEND_OK, GONE, /cannot|can't|unable|already|too much/i)).to_s
  if r =~ SEND_OK
    points, drained = $1.to_i, $2
    seen = $demonmana_cap && $demonmana_cap[:id] == d[:id] ? $demonmana_cap : {}
    $demonmana_cap = { id: d[:id], points: [points, seen[:points].to_i].max, said: seen[:said] }
    echo "demon holds #{points} mana now (#{drained} drained)."
  elsif r =~ GONE
    echo "couldn't find your #{d[:noun]} to send mana to."
  else
    echo "send said: #{r.strip[0, 120].empty? ? 'nothing' : r.strip[0, 120]}"
  end
end

def get_mana
  if $demonmana_missed_at && Time.now.to_f - $demonmana_missed_at < GET_RETRY_AFTER
    $demonmana_taken = false   # too soon to call it again; keep the once-a-hunt latch open
    return
  end
  # 11/27: never stall a fight (an attack script waits on us; in Reim that includes the Emperor)
  fighting = Array(GameObj.targets).any? { |t| t && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
  d = demon(fighting ? 0 : GET_WAIT)
  return unless d
  return skip_note(d) if low_capacity?(d)
  unless d[:here]
    $demonmana_missed_at = Time.now.to_f
    $demonmana_taken = false
    return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here -- can't ask it for mana yet (will call it again in #{GET_RETRY_AFTER}s).")
  end
  $demonmana_missed_at = nil
  waitrt?
  r = dothistimeout("tell mdemon send 50", 4, Regexp.union(GOT_MANA, GONE, /has no mana|any mana|nothing to send/i)).to_s
  if r =~ GOT_MANA
    echo "got #{$1} mana back from the demon."
  else
    echo "no mana from the demon (#{r.strip[0, 100].empty? ? 'no answer' : r.strip[0, 100]})."
  end
end

case script.vars[1].to_s.downcase
when 'send' then send_mana
when 'get'  then get_mana
else echo "usage: ;demonmana send   |   ;demonmana get"
end
